WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.669
[music playing]

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.043
[thud]

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.010
[panting]

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.012
[thud]

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.847
[thud]

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:14.681
[thud]

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:15.582
Ah.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.983
[thud]

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.953
[cracking]

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.322
[branches crunching]

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:25.725
Excellent work,
[inaudible] Sal.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.127
Come with me.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.429
There are more that need
to be pulled from the sky.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.764
This way.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.267
[birds singing]

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.173
I might be of help if you
tell me what you're looking for.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.308
A span of trees.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.610
What sort of trees?

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:47.747
Ones that will hold
and reign over the rest.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.581
This is not that.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.049
Do you agree?

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.051
That depends.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.987
Yes.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.188
So much depends.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.606
Yes.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:14.240
Yes.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.208
This is the place.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.744
I'm sure of it.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:23.850
Do you see how these
create a perfect form?

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.152
Yes?

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.654
Leave them.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.022
Clear the rest.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.256
What are we building?

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:34.060
A sky table-- these
will be the legs.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:34.961
Sky table?

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.429
Yes.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:41.034
I wish to stride over the
trees and study the clouds

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.735
and the smoke from [inaudible].

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:47.140
No man in New France
will possess such a view.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.741
I have never heard
of such a thing.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:49.576
I have invented it.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:54.881
I have made a sketch.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:02.121
There is no precedent
for such a thing.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.191
[inaudible] at once.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.928
I have been granted a
wife by decree of the king.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:12.866
And I wish to complete the table
before we are properly bound.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.968
What of Marie?

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.604
Marie is not my wife.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.438
Sir.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.877
Worry not, 'tis
the [inaudible]..

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.711
Bonjour!

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:29.782
Ah.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:38.391
Tell me, Sal, what does
a man such as yourself

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:44.697
think of all day, besides
the bite of the axe, I mean?

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.132
I think of nothing.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.300
Nonsense.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.402
The bird of thought
enters us all.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:53.773
What vapors fill your mind?

00:02:53.840 --> 00:03:00.647
[sighs] I think sometimes,
uh, of my brother.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.949
He who is dead?

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.083
Yes.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.486
This is what
families are like.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.923
The ones who have come
and passed from this world

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.824
push us to find new fields.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:16.963
It is the fear of departing this
realm without leaving a mark.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.433
You must do better
than this dead brother.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.335
You must set a
course for yourself.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.740
I will start with this.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:36.416
And Marie must not
know a word of this.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:40.720
Now I need to be
able to trust you.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.889
You have my word.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.490
Good.

